sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-05> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-05--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-05--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch16-05: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.57" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.572"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.58"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Trabecular orientation and a finite-element stress map are both computable with existing methods, and some open micro-CT already resolves individual trabeculae. The classic crane comparison needs an intact loaded bone, which is less often deposited than small plugs. Because the stress field depends on boundary conditions that are not in the same files, agreement is informative and still open to circular loading assumptions." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: From micro-CT, extract trabecular orientations in the femoral head and compare them with principal-stress trajectories from a finite-element model of the same bone under stance loads, including a test that the two families cross near 90 degrees. Alignment well above a randomized or isotropic fabric would support the claim; a weak correlation or non-orthogonal crossings would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Principal-stress directions change with the assumed joint loads, so a model can be tuned toward the anatomy.", "Many open micro-CT volumes are excised cylinders rather than intact femoral heads under physiological boundary conditions." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch16-05--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch16-05--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-05--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch16-05 by Grok 4.7: 0.76" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-05--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-05> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-05--grok--operationalizability> .
